<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    Better Traders Guild - Agrihand farming duty.

    Priority order (each node only reached when the one above returns no job):
      1. Harvest mature food crops from in-range hydroponics basins (yield drops
         forbidden, since the mech is not the player faction).
      2. Haul that produce to the nearest in-range shelf (stays forbidden); if no
         shelf has room it is left on the floor, already forbidden.
      3. Sow the basin's crop (rice in the BTG greenhouse) into emptied basin cells.
      4. Plant a random decorative flower in any empty plant pot anywhere in the
         settlement (structure-wide, not just the greenhouse - see JobGiver_BTGAgrihandPlantPots).
      5. Once the pot round is done, walk back to the home room / anchor point.
      6. Return near the anchor point and dormant self-charge until a crop matures.

    The farm work (1-3) is confined to the mech's greenhouse room (see FarmArea); the
    pot planting (4) ranges across the whole settlement structure footprint
    (StructureBoundsCache), so the mech paths pot-to-pot between rooms but always returns
    home (5) to sleep where its primary rice-farming duty re-triggers. Used by
    LordJob_MechFarm.
  -->

  <DutyDef>
    <defName>BTG_MechFarm</defName>
    <thinkNode Class="ThinkNode_Priority">
      <subNodes>
        <li Class="BetterTradersGuild.AI.Mechs.JobGiver_BTGAgrihandHarvest" />
        <li Class="BetterTradersGuild.AI.Mechs.JobGiver_BTGAgrihandHaul" />
        <li Class="BetterTradersGuild.AI.Mechs.JobGiver_BTGAgrihandSow" />
        <li Class="BetterTradersGuild.AI.Mechs.JobGiver_BTGAgrihandPlantPots" />
        <li Class="BetterTradersGuild.AI.Mechs.JobGiver_BTGAgrihandReturnHome" />
        <li Class="BetterTradersGuild.AI.Mechs.JobGiver_BTGAgrihandStandby" />
      </subNodes>
    </thinkNode>
  </DutyDef>

</Defs>
